1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,503
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:05,714
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,508 --> 00:00:10,844
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:12,887
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,268
[in English] Today is the day you die.

7
00:00:18,351 --> 00:00:19,602
[in English] And I'm a man of my word!

8
00:00:19,686 --> 00:00:21,312
[Uno, in English] <i>Sir, I have the keys</i>
<i>of the bait vehicle.</i>

9
00:00:21,396 --> 00:00:23,982
[in English] I'll be approaching
in 20 minutes or less.

10
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:25,734
[Olga] <i>I know how to fight.</i>

11
00:00:25,817 --> 00:00:26,651
- Okay.
- Huh?

12
00:00:26,735 --> 00:00:28,028
Not that you asked,

13
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:31,197
but I guested as a goon
in <i>Hearts on the Badge</i>.

14
00:00:31,281 --> 00:00:32,240
Through the main entrance!

15
00:00:32,323 --> 00:00:33,533
Where's your helper?

16
00:00:33,616 --> 00:00:34,868
He said it's his birthday.

17
00:00:35,535 --> 00:00:36,911
[goon 1] <i>It's not Jaymar's birthday today.</i>

18
00:00:36,995 --> 00:00:38,496
PREVIOUSLY

19
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:42,167
[in English] I'm going to execute
both of you in front of the camera

20
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:44,794
and send it to the armed forces.

21
00:00:44,878 --> 00:00:47,839
[in English] So that they'll know
that I am serious.

22
00:00:47,922 --> 00:00:49,466
[Paldo] <i>Atoy is family.</i>

23
00:00:49,549 --> 00:00:50,508
Now he needs help,

24
00:00:50,592 --> 00:00:51,426
will you all be cowards?

25
00:00:51,509 --> 00:00:52,594
All right, let's fight!

26
00:00:52,677 --> 00:00:53,678
- Charge!
- Charge?

27
00:00:53,762 --> 00:00:54,721
- Let's go! All right!
- Charge!

28
00:00:54,804 --> 00:00:56,598
[clamoring]

29
00:00:56,681 --> 00:00:58,641
All right, all right!

30
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:00,268
Brad, I'll take over. You go outside.

31
00:01:00,351 --> 00:01:01,394
[thumping and swishing]

32
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:03,271
[grunting and groaning]

33
00:01:07,984 --> 00:01:09,611
[Uno] <i>No visual of Padua.</i>

34
00:01:09,694 --> 00:01:11,029
- [gunshots]
- [in English] <i>But I'm under heavy attack!</i>

35
00:01:11,112 --> 00:01:12,655
I need immediate backup.

36
00:01:12,739 --> 00:01:14,365
[gunshots]

37
00:01:14,991 --> 00:01:15,950
[Lily] <i>Atoy, what now? Where do we go?</i>

38
00:01:16,618 --> 00:01:17,577
[Atoy] <i>We'll find another way. Let's go.</i>

39
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:18,870
You think you can escape?

40
00:01:18,953 --> 00:01:20,622
- [thuds]
- [groans]

41
00:01:20,705 --> 00:01:23,208
[grunting and groaning]

42
00:01:23,291 --> 00:01:24,125
[thumping and thudding]

43
00:01:24,709 --> 00:01:26,211
[Ame] <i>That's why you're not Atoy's child!</i>

44
00:01:26,294 --> 00:01:29,047
You probably got that attitude
from your real parents!

45
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:30,340
[Janine] <i>You're my mommy, right?!</i>

46
00:01:30,423 --> 00:01:32,300
Janine, let's talk first.

47
00:01:32,884 --> 00:01:33,968
[in English] No!

48
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:38,097
[music swells]

49
00:01:40,433 --> 00:01:45,480
Sister Ame, you should have
controlled yourself.

50
00:01:46,981 --> 00:01:50,276
Because I still feel sorry for Janine.

51
00:01:51,569 --> 00:01:53,571
I'm sorry.

52
00:01:54,322 --> 00:01:57,909
I just couldn't control myself.

53
00:01:57,992 --> 00:01:59,619
She's so annoying.

54
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:03,540
But fate really plays differently,
doesn't it?

55
00:02:04,165 --> 00:02:06,918
Before she teased you
for not having parents.

56
00:02:07,544 --> 00:02:09,254
In the end, it's her who doesn't have one.

57
00:02:13,091 --> 00:02:14,217
[Ibyang] Janine.

58
00:02:18,847 --> 00:02:20,723
[melancholic music playing]

59
00:02:20,807 --> 00:02:21,850
Janine.

60
00:02:23,184 --> 00:02:24,185
[in English] It's okay.

61
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:25,895
Ibyang, leave her alone for now.

62
00:02:27,897 --> 00:02:30,942
I want to comfort her.

63
00:02:31,025 --> 00:02:33,278
I want to tell her

64
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:35,572
everything will be okay.

65
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:38,324
Because

66
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:42,495
I know the feeling of having no parents.

67
00:02:42,579 --> 00:02:43,454
[sobs]

68
00:02:49,127 --> 00:02:51,004
[sobs] Thank you.

69
00:02:52,005 --> 00:02:53,923
You're really so kind.

70
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:59,554
You have such a beautiful heart, Ibyang.

71
00:03:03,182 --> 00:03:06,144
Aunt Audrey, what about you?

72
00:03:06,227 --> 00:03:07,854
Are you okay?

73
00:03:08,688 --> 00:03:13,109
Because surely it hurts

74
00:03:13,192 --> 00:03:19,324
to hear that Janine
isn't really your child.

75
00:03:20,199 --> 00:03:21,159
You know,

76
00:03:22,368 --> 00:03:26,873
you might be the first person
to ask me how I am.

77
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:30,752
[in English] Thank you.

78
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:32,921
[in English] I've been better.

79
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:35,757
[sobs] But didn't you say…

80
00:03:37,675 --> 00:03:39,177
everything will be okay?

81
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:41,512
[melodramatic music playing]

82
00:03:41,596 --> 00:03:43,181
[Ame] Audrey.

83
00:03:43,264 --> 00:03:45,225
Audrey, I'm really sorry.

84
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:47,602
I didn't mean it.

85
00:03:48,561 --> 00:03:50,605
Don't worry about it, Ame.

86
00:03:51,898 --> 00:03:52,774
Maybe

87
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:57,612
fate found a way for Janine
to learn the truth.

88
00:03:57,695 --> 00:03:59,155
[music fades]

89
00:03:59,239 --> 00:04:00,782
[breath quivers] I just hope…

90
00:04:02,325 --> 00:04:05,328
Atoy and I will be able to find
our real daughter.

91
00:04:05,411 --> 00:04:06,829
[melodramatic music playing]

92
00:04:06,913 --> 00:04:08,581
Don't worry.

93
00:04:09,791 --> 00:04:11,876
You'll find her too.

94
00:04:12,961 --> 00:04:15,505
You and Tatoy will have a complete family.

95
00:04:25,932 --> 00:04:26,891
[Audrey] I hope so.

96
00:04:31,271 --> 00:04:35,900
[suave theme music playing]

97
00:05:03,678 --> 00:05:05,388
[clamoring]

98
00:05:05,471 --> 00:05:06,431
- [action music playing]
- Charge! Charge!

99
00:05:06,514 --> 00:05:07,390
- [Paldo] Faster!
- [Emerson] Okay!

100
00:05:07,473 --> 00:05:09,225
- [T-Bak] Wait a minute.
- This is it. This is it.

101
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:10,351
Let's go.

102
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:13,396
[music fades]

103
00:05:13,479 --> 00:05:14,605
[gunshots]

104
00:05:15,773 --> 00:05:17,275
[screaming and panicking]

105
00:05:17,358 --> 00:05:19,527
Gunfire! Gunfire!

106
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:20,903
Gunfire! Gu--

107
00:05:20,987 --> 00:05:23,656
- [gunshots]
- [action music playing]

108
00:05:25,074 --> 00:05:26,492
[gunshots]

109
00:05:26,576 --> 00:05:27,535
Wait!

110
00:05:27,618 --> 00:05:28,953
Why are there guns?!

111
00:05:29,037 --> 00:05:30,496
I can't handle that!

112
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:32,540
Me too! I thought
it was just fistfighting.

113
00:05:32,623 --> 00:05:34,959
But if there are guns, I can't do it!

114
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:36,419
- Oh.
- Let's call for backup!

115
00:05:36,502 --> 00:05:38,296
Maybe… Maybe there's
a nearby police station!

116
00:05:38,379 --> 00:05:40,048
[in English] Oh,
there's no police station!

117
00:05:40,131 --> 00:05:42,175
The road is long, and we haven't seen one.

118
00:05:42,258 --> 00:05:44,510
So? We're not charging?

119
00:05:44,594 --> 00:05:45,595
I'm charging.

120
00:05:45,678 --> 00:05:47,555
I don't want anything
to happen to Brother Atoy.

121
00:05:47,638 --> 00:05:48,681
Karla!

122
00:05:48,765 --> 00:05:50,558
- Karla!
- Karla, wait!

123
00:05:50,641 --> 00:05:52,310
[T-Bak] It's dangerous inside!

124
00:05:52,393 --> 00:05:54,145
You could die!

125
00:05:54,228 --> 00:05:56,355
It's okay! I don't care!

126
00:05:56,439 --> 00:05:58,566
As long as my brother doesn't get hurt!

127
00:05:58,649 --> 00:05:59,734
- Bro-
- Brother?

128
00:05:59,817 --> 00:06:00,693
Brother? Wait.

129
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:01,861
Ouch.

130
00:06:01,944 --> 00:06:03,029
Brother?

131
00:06:03,112 --> 00:06:04,072
Brother?!

132
00:06:04,155 --> 00:06:05,406
Yes, Karla and Brother Atoy are siblings.

133
00:06:05,490 --> 00:06:06,991
Ah! I'll explain later!

134
00:06:07,075 --> 00:06:08,534
For now, I'm going to Brother Atoy!

135
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:09,786
- Karla! Karla!
- Karla, wait for me!

136
00:06:09,869 --> 00:06:10,703
Gavin!

137
00:06:11,829 --> 00:06:12,705
What?!

138
00:06:12,789 --> 00:06:13,623
Atoy will kill us.

139
00:06:13,706 --> 00:06:14,707
Are we just going to stand here?!

140
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:15,958
Huh?

141
00:06:16,042 --> 00:06:18,878
The reason we came here is to rescue Atoy.

142
00:06:18,961 --> 00:06:20,004
Do or die!

143
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:21,214
- Until the end!
- [shouting]

144
00:06:21,297 --> 00:06:22,131
End!

145
00:06:22,215 --> 00:06:23,633
- We'll all charge!
- We'll charge!

146
00:06:23,716 --> 00:06:25,593
- Are you ready?!
- Charge! Charge! Charge!

147
00:06:25,676 --> 00:06:26,886
- Charge!
- Let's go!

148
00:06:26,969 --> 00:06:28,471
Let's go.

149
00:06:28,554 --> 00:06:30,098
- Charge!
- Let's go, let's go!

150
00:06:30,181 --> 00:06:31,599
- Okay!
- Let's go.

151
00:06:31,682 --> 00:06:32,934
Wait. Why does it seem like
no one's moving?

152
00:06:33,017 --> 00:06:34,393
- Uh…
- What's wrong with you? What--

153
00:06:34,477 --> 00:06:35,978
What's this? Am I just hyping myself up?

154
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:37,105
- Uh, Emerson, you know,
- Huh?

155
00:06:37,188 --> 00:06:38,439
I have a good plan.

156
00:06:38,523 --> 00:06:40,733
- What?
- Here's what you do.

157
00:06:40,817 --> 00:06:42,777
- Go inside.
- Right.

158
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:44,362
See how many enemies there are.

159
00:06:44,445 --> 00:06:45,988
Right!

160
00:06:46,072 --> 00:06:47,949
Yes, right. I'll check
if we're outnumbered or not.

161
00:06:48,032 --> 00:06:49,867
- Okay.
- Then--

162
00:06:49,951 --> 00:06:51,702
- Just look inside.
- Then?

163
00:06:51,786 --> 00:06:52,829
- Then?
- Then call us.

164
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:54,497
- Right! Right!
- Yes. Right, right, right.

165
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:55,665
Yes. That's good, that's good.

166
00:06:55,748 --> 00:06:56,749
- [overlapping chatter]
- You can do it, Brother Emerson!

167
00:06:56,833 --> 00:06:58,084
You can do it!

168
00:06:58,167 --> 00:07:00,336
We believe in you, Brother Emerson!

169
00:07:00,419 --> 00:07:01,671
Why don't you do it instead?

170
00:07:01,754 --> 00:07:02,839
- Not me, not me!
- I have a stiff neck, huh!

171
00:07:02,922 --> 00:07:03,756
Not me-- Not me, brother!

172
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:04,841
- I might get high blood too!
- I don't think I can!

173
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:05,758
Go, Emerson!

174
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:06,676
- [overlapping chatter] You can do it!
- Yes, you can do it.

175
00:07:06,759 --> 00:07:08,094
- I can do it? I can do it?
- You can do it!

176
00:07:08,177 --> 00:07:10,012
- [cheering] Go, Brother Emerson!
- Go, Emerson!

177
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:11,180
[cheering] Come on! Go!

178
00:07:11,264 --> 00:07:12,390
- I can't do it! I can't do it!
- [clamoring]

179
00:07:12,473 --> 00:07:13,766
Come with me!

180
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:15,935
- Oh! Go, go, go, go, go!
- Go now!

181
00:07:16,018 --> 00:07:17,645
- There it is!
- There might be more gunfire!

182
00:07:17,728 --> 00:07:19,147
Brother Emerson!

183
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:20,064
I don't think I can!

184
00:07:20,148 --> 00:07:21,732
You can do it!

185
00:07:21,816 --> 00:07:23,734
Brother Emerson, don't die!

186
00:07:23,818 --> 00:07:25,403
- Don't meddle!
- He can handle it!

187
00:07:25,486 --> 00:07:27,405
- Your hand stinks!
- [in English] Sorry.

188
00:07:27,488 --> 00:07:30,324
[tense music playing]

189
00:07:34,787 --> 00:07:35,872
[grunts]

190
00:07:35,955 --> 00:07:37,999
Uh, uh…

191
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:42,128
[foreboding music playing]

192
00:07:42,211 --> 00:07:44,547
- [thumps]
- [grunting]

193
00:07:44,630 --> 00:07:45,840
[gunshots]

194
00:07:45,923 --> 00:07:47,049
[Emerson] Help me!

195
00:07:47,133 --> 00:07:48,676
[gunshots]

196
00:07:48,759 --> 00:07:50,094
[grunting] Help!

197
00:07:50,178 --> 00:07:51,387
Help! No, no!

198
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:53,139
[grunts]

199
00:07:53,222 --> 00:07:54,682
- Help!
- [thumps]

200
00:07:55,475 --> 00:07:57,351
[grunting and groaning]

201
00:07:57,435 --> 00:07:58,686
[thumping and thudding]

202
00:07:59,937 --> 00:08:00,938
[gasps]

203
00:08:01,022 --> 00:08:02,356
- [pants]
- Are you okay, Emerson?

204
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:04,400
- I'm fine.
- [tense music playing]

205
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:05,318
Emerson!

206
00:08:05,401 --> 00:08:06,486
- [grunting]
- [gunshots]

207
00:08:06,569 --> 00:08:07,862
What?!

208
00:08:07,945 --> 00:08:09,238
They went there?!

209
00:08:09,906 --> 00:08:12,783
Are they so angry at the world
that they'd risk their lives?!

210
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:15,578
Maybe they just really wanted to help.

211
00:08:15,661 --> 00:08:16,787
But don't worry.

212
00:08:16,871 --> 00:08:19,040
I already called the police
to follow them.

213
00:08:19,123 --> 00:08:22,168
If I could do something, I'd join them.

214
00:08:22,251 --> 00:08:24,712
But I might get

215
00:08:24,795 --> 00:08:26,088
an arthritis attack.

216
00:08:26,172 --> 00:08:27,215
I'd just be a burden.

217
00:08:27,298 --> 00:08:29,467
I'm not as strong as your child, Cita.

218
00:08:30,051 --> 00:08:31,052
What did you say?!

219
00:08:31,844 --> 00:08:33,471
Karla went with them?!

220
00:08:33,554 --> 00:08:36,474
Son of a thread, this child, really!

221
00:08:36,557 --> 00:08:37,642
Yes. They couldn't stop her.

222
00:08:37,725 --> 00:08:39,936
She said she loves her Brother Atoy.

223
00:08:40,019 --> 00:08:44,065
As if the one in danger
is really her sibling, huh?

224
00:08:44,148 --> 00:08:46,234
Well, Atoy really is her sibling.

225
00:08:46,317 --> 00:08:48,444
My God. I hope they'll be safe.

226
00:08:48,528 --> 00:08:49,737
[dramatic sting]

227
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:52,114
Um, Cita, please repeat
what you said earlier.

228
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:53,157
That's it.

229
00:08:53,241 --> 00:08:54,367
Let's just pray for them.

230
00:08:55,034 --> 00:08:56,410
My God. What is this?

231
00:08:56,494 --> 00:08:58,663
- [tense music playing]
- Real sibling, she said?

232
00:09:02,708 --> 00:09:04,502
[music swells]

233
00:09:04,585 --> 00:09:06,045
[music fades]

234
00:09:06,128 --> 00:09:09,590
[rousing music playing]

235
00:09:09,674 --> 00:09:13,386
[gunshots]

236
00:09:13,469 --> 00:09:16,597
- [tense music playing]
- [gunshots]

237
00:09:22,228 --> 00:09:23,813
[heavy breathing]

238
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:42,206
[heavy breathing]

239
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:51,173
Atoy! [echoing]

240
00:09:53,092 --> 00:09:55,261
[music swells]

241
00:09:55,344 --> 00:09:56,387
[gunshot]

242
00:10:01,934 --> 00:10:07,607
[sneaky music playing]

243
00:10:10,109 --> 00:10:13,821
[whispering indistinctly]

244
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:26,709
[gasps]

245
00:10:27,918 --> 00:10:28,919
[quirky sting]

246
00:10:29,003 --> 00:10:29,837
[whispers] You too.

247
00:10:31,297 --> 00:10:34,008
[whispering]

248
00:10:34,091 --> 00:10:39,263
[sneaky music playing]

249
00:10:45,936 --> 00:10:49,106
[quirky sting]

250
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:50,608
[inaudible] Your turn.

251
00:10:56,989 --> 00:10:58,157
[whimpering]

252
00:10:58,240 --> 00:11:00,368
[whispering indistinctly]

253
00:11:00,451 --> 00:11:01,869
[whispers] You go first.

254
00:11:02,453 --> 00:11:05,790
[whispers] Go ahead.

255
00:11:14,298 --> 00:11:18,219
[tense music playing]

256
00:11:18,302 --> 00:11:21,847
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

257
00:11:26,894 --> 00:11:28,771
- [grunts and groans]
- [squeals]

258
00:11:28,854 --> 00:11:30,815
That's really going to fire!

259
00:11:30,898 --> 00:11:32,149
It will fire!

260
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:34,360
[T-Bak wails] It will fire! It will--

261
00:11:34,443 --> 00:11:35,277
[T-Bak wailing]

262
00:11:35,361 --> 00:11:36,237
[overlapping chatter]

263
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:37,696
[grunts]

264
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:39,115
You jerk!

265
00:11:39,198 --> 00:11:40,366
- [groans]
- I told you it would fire!

266
00:11:40,449 --> 00:11:42,368
You jerk! I was already scared!

267
00:11:42,451 --> 00:11:44,453
- [groans]
- And you still won't stop, huh!

268
00:11:44,537 --> 00:11:46,163
- Ouch--
- Oh!

269
00:11:46,247 --> 00:11:47,873
- Why don't you--
- [shouts]

270
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:48,833
[clamoring nearby]

271
00:11:48,916 --> 00:11:50,626
[indistinct chattering]

272
00:11:50,709 --> 00:11:51,544
[gun cocks]

273
00:11:51,627 --> 00:11:53,170
- [grunts]
- [screams]

274
00:11:53,254 --> 00:11:54,296
Oh, he's gonna fire it!

275
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:56,048
- [wails]
- Brother Kurt, stop that!

276
00:11:56,132 --> 00:11:57,007
[gasps]

277
00:11:57,091 --> 00:11:58,467
- [sneaky music playing]
- Put it down, put it down.

278
00:11:58,551 --> 00:12:01,262
[gasping and panting]

279
00:12:01,846 --> 00:12:02,805
No one got hit?

280
00:12:02,888 --> 00:12:04,140
- It was wrong to play
- No one got hit?

281
00:12:04,223 --> 00:12:05,516
with toy guns.

282
00:12:05,599 --> 00:12:07,184
- Let's go there. Let's go.
- [T-Bak panting]

283
00:12:07,268 --> 00:12:08,394
Huh?

284
00:12:08,477 --> 00:12:09,478
That should be fine.

285
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:13,149
[whimpers]

286
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:15,234
[indistinct chattering]

287
00:12:17,736 --> 00:12:22,950
[tense music playing]

288
00:12:26,203 --> 00:12:27,121
[gunshot]

289
00:12:28,372 --> 00:12:29,707
[clangs]

290
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:32,209
- [intense music playing]
- Atoy! [echoing]

291
00:12:32,293 --> 00:12:36,130
[music swells]

292
00:12:36,213 --> 00:12:37,381
[tense music playing]

293
00:12:38,132 --> 00:12:40,551
[gunshots]

294
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:08,037
[machine whirring]

295
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:12,082
[music swells]

296
00:13:26,847 --> 00:13:29,099
- [Samir, in English] Let's go, let's go.
- Distract them.

297
00:13:29,183 --> 00:13:30,017
- Okay.
- [Samir, in English] It's time

298
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:32,019
to meet your maker.

299
00:13:32,811 --> 00:13:33,771
Hey, American!

300
00:13:33,854 --> 00:13:34,980
Look here!

301
00:13:35,064 --> 00:13:36,857
Put Brother Atoy down!

302
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:38,067
[speaks in Russian] Shut your mouth!

303
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:40,402
[Karla] Put him down! What?!

304
00:13:40,486 --> 00:13:41,570
You won't?!

305
00:13:41,654 --> 00:13:44,240
1v1, come here! Hey!

306
00:13:44,323 --> 00:13:46,450
Go, Gavin! You can do it!

307
00:13:46,534 --> 00:13:48,410
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

308
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:50,788
[Karla] Put Brother Atoy down! Okay!

309
00:13:51,789 --> 00:13:53,541
Go, Gavin! Go! You can do it!

310
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,336
- [grunts]
- [Karla] Gavin! Be careful!

311
00:13:58,254 --> 00:14:00,297
[Karla grunts]

312
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:01,674
[Karla gasps]

313
00:14:02,758 --> 00:14:04,510
[grunts and groans]

314
00:14:17,731 --> 00:14:18,691
[Karla] Gavin!

315
00:14:22,486 --> 00:14:24,572
[metal clangs]

316
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:34,206
[music fades]

317
00:14:36,876 --> 00:14:38,294
[panicking]

318
00:14:38,377 --> 00:14:40,004
Brother Emerson, are you okay?

319
00:14:40,087 --> 00:14:41,630
- [shushing]
- They didn't hurt you?

320
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:42,923
Hey! You're too noisy!

321
00:14:43,007 --> 00:14:45,175
- [shushes]
- [shrieks]

322
00:14:45,259 --> 00:14:46,510
Don't be noisy.

323
00:14:46,594 --> 00:14:48,053
- Don't be noisy.
- [Jona] Emerson!

324
00:14:49,179 --> 00:14:50,931
- [screaming]
- Emerson!

325
00:14:51,015 --> 00:14:52,224
[shushes] You're too noisy!

326
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:54,101
Hey. Don't be noisy.

327
00:14:54,184 --> 00:14:55,436
Someone-- Someone's chasing me.

328
00:14:55,519 --> 00:14:57,438
- They're chasing me.
- Another one?

329
00:14:57,521 --> 00:14:59,440
Yes. Come here. They have guns! Let's go.

330
00:14:59,523 --> 00:15:01,191
Let's go, let's go.
There are many of them.

331
00:15:01,275 --> 00:15:02,192
There are many of them. Let's get out!

332
00:15:02,276 --> 00:15:03,485
Here, this way!

333
00:15:03,569 --> 00:15:07,072
[action music playing]

334
00:15:08,866 --> 00:15:10,826
- [music fades]
- [gun cocks]

335
00:15:14,163 --> 00:15:15,414
Alcaraz.

336
00:15:15,497 --> 00:15:16,790
Good to see you alive, sir.

337
00:15:16,874 --> 00:15:18,417
Thank you. Where's Lily?

338
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:21,211
[footsteps approaching]

339
00:15:21,295 --> 00:15:22,713
She's Lily.

340
00:15:23,297 --> 00:15:24,173
She's the decoder.

341
00:15:25,841 --> 00:15:26,842
Atoy, thank you.

342
00:15:26,926 --> 00:15:27,927
Thank you, all of you.

343
00:15:28,510 --> 00:15:29,678
[in English] Good job, Alcaraz.

344
00:15:29,762 --> 00:15:31,138
We need to secure Lily.

345
00:15:31,221 --> 00:15:32,848
She might be targeted again.

346
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:35,059
I'll take care of Lily Santiago, sir.

347
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:36,310
[Atoy, in English] Okay.

348
00:15:36,393 --> 00:15:37,561
What about Samir?

349
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:39,188
He escaped.

350
00:15:39,271 --> 00:15:41,440
So, you should call
Colonel Mercado immediately.

351
00:15:41,523 --> 00:15:43,192
Tell him about Samir

352
00:15:43,275 --> 00:15:45,110
and about the ambassador of Zahran.

353
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:46,612
- [in English] On it, sir.
- [Atoy, in English] Okay.

354
00:15:47,196 --> 00:15:50,824
[pensive music playing]

355
00:15:50,908 --> 00:15:52,159
Good thing you're safe, Brother.

356
00:15:52,242 --> 00:15:53,327
[Uno, in English] Good job.

357
00:15:53,410 --> 00:15:54,244
[Atoy] Wait, little sister.

358
00:15:55,079 --> 00:15:56,580
How are you? Were you hurt?

359
00:15:56,664 --> 00:15:57,748
[Karla] Not really.

360
00:15:58,624 --> 00:15:59,541
[Atoy] Hmm?

361
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:02,503
[sighs] How are you?

362
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:04,004
I'm okay.

363
00:16:04,588 --> 00:16:05,673
Are you okay, Gavin?

364
00:16:06,256 --> 00:16:07,841
You had to tag along.

365
00:16:07,925 --> 00:16:09,718
I just wanted to help.

366
00:16:09,802 --> 00:16:11,428
But I'm fine.

367
00:16:13,555 --> 00:16:14,515
'Toy!

368
00:16:15,766 --> 00:16:17,184
- 'Toy.
- Paldo.

369
00:16:18,852 --> 00:16:19,895
Atoy.

370
00:16:20,479 --> 00:16:21,647
- [man] Brother Atoy.
- [T-Bak] Hi, brother!

371
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:23,524
Oh? Ha--

372
00:16:23,607 --> 00:16:24,733
What are you doing here?

373
00:16:24,817 --> 00:16:26,443
Atoy, huh. Are you impressed?

374
00:16:26,527 --> 00:16:28,821
See? We defeated the enemies.

375
00:16:28,904 --> 00:16:30,656
- [chuckling]
- We-- We toppled them.

376
00:16:30,739 --> 00:16:32,491
We just got lucky!

377
00:16:32,574 --> 00:16:34,076
What-- What are you doing here?

378
00:16:34,159 --> 00:16:35,911
What if something happened to you?

379
00:16:35,995 --> 00:16:37,329
What if one of you died?

380
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:39,915
Ouch. We got scolded.

381
00:16:39,999 --> 00:16:42,334
No. Of course, I'm just worried.

382
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:43,794
I don't want anything bad to happen to you

383
00:16:43,877 --> 00:16:46,547
because you're my responsibility.

384
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:48,007
I don't want anything bad
to happen to you…

385
00:16:48,090 --> 00:16:49,717
Of course, I love you.

386
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,218
[teasing]

387
00:16:51,844 --> 00:16:54,013
So, you love us, Brother Atoy!

388
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:55,055
Of course.

389
00:16:55,139 --> 00:16:56,181
You love us, right?

390
00:16:56,265 --> 00:16:57,307
Of course, you're my family.

391
00:16:57,391 --> 00:16:59,518
[teasing]

392
00:16:59,601 --> 00:17:02,146
Group hug! Group hug!

393
00:17:02,229 --> 00:17:06,442
[whooping]

394
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:08,777
[T-Bak] Ouch! Ouch! Ouch! Ouch!

395
00:17:08,861 --> 00:17:14,950
[suave theme music playing]

396
00:17:48,567 --> 00:17:49,526
Godmother?

397
00:17:50,152 --> 00:17:52,071
- [Olga] Atoy! Atoy! Atoy!
- Ibyang--

398
00:17:52,154 --> 00:17:53,030
- [Atoy] Oh?
- [squeals]

399
00:17:53,113 --> 00:17:53,947
[Atoy] Olga.

400
00:17:54,531 --> 00:17:55,574
Good thing you're safe.

401
00:17:55,657 --> 00:17:57,534
Uh, uh… What are you doing here?

402
00:17:57,618 --> 00:17:59,161
Eh, eh…

403
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:02,039
I was supposed to join the rescue for you
at the junkyard,

404
00:18:02,122 --> 00:18:03,123
but Uno…

405
00:18:03,207 --> 00:18:04,291
[sighs]

406
00:18:04,374 --> 00:18:06,210
He's terrible company.

407
00:18:06,293 --> 00:18:07,711
He sent me away!

408
00:18:07,795 --> 00:18:10,089
I was all ready to save you.

409
00:18:10,672 --> 00:18:13,467
It's better you didn't.
You might have gotten hurt.

410
00:18:13,550 --> 00:18:14,384
Oh, thank you.

411
00:18:14,468 --> 00:18:16,720
Eh, are Ibyang and the others here?

412
00:18:16,804 --> 00:18:18,222
Where are Godmother Cita and the rest?

413
00:18:18,305 --> 00:18:19,598
Did you see them?

414
00:18:20,182 --> 00:18:22,017
Ah, no. No one's here.

415
00:18:22,101 --> 00:18:23,393
They're at the church.

416
00:18:23,477 --> 00:18:25,020
Church?

417
00:18:25,104 --> 00:18:27,648
- Oh, all right. Thank you.
- Oh. Wait, wait, Atoy. Hold on.

418
00:18:29,399 --> 00:18:30,359
Um…

419
00:18:31,443 --> 00:18:32,694
[sharp exhale]

420
00:18:33,695 --> 00:18:35,656
- [Atoy] What?
- Here it is.

421
00:18:37,157 --> 00:18:38,659
Hold on tight.

422
00:18:40,369 --> 00:18:41,703
You might not be able to handle it.

423
00:18:43,122 --> 00:18:44,373
Why? Did something happen?

424
00:18:44,456 --> 00:18:45,541
Eh, no. Nothing.

425
00:18:45,624 --> 00:18:46,458
[Atoy] Oh?

426
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:48,627
Don't-- Don't worry. It's good news.

427
00:18:49,169 --> 00:18:50,087
- [in English] Promise.
- Mm-hmm.

428
00:18:50,170 --> 00:18:51,004
‪[Olga sighs]

429
00:18:52,089 --> 00:18:52,923
Uh…

430
00:18:53,006 --> 00:18:55,551
[mellow music playing]

431
00:18:59,513 --> 00:19:01,056
[Olga] Ibyang made that.

432
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:04,852
She told me

433
00:19:05,769 --> 00:19:09,022
that when I return, we'll be whole again.

434
00:19:11,692 --> 00:19:12,609
Oh.

435
00:19:12,693 --> 00:19:13,610
[Olga] But…

436
00:19:15,028 --> 00:19:16,155
I don't deserve that.

437
00:19:17,072 --> 00:19:18,657
Why not?

438
00:19:19,658 --> 00:19:20,909
Oh, isn't it…

439
00:19:21,743 --> 00:19:22,578
You're her mother, right?

440
00:19:22,661 --> 00:19:24,288
Oh, why-- why would you say that?

441
00:19:24,371 --> 00:19:27,791
[music fades]

442
00:19:33,130 --> 00:19:35,257
You're Ibyang's real father.

443
00:19:36,758 --> 00:19:38,010
She's your child, Atoy.

444
00:19:39,178 --> 00:19:41,597
[music intensifies]

445
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:42,556
What?

446
00:19:43,265 --> 00:19:44,141
Me?

447
00:19:47,519 --> 00:19:48,687
What are you saying?

448
00:19:48,770 --> 00:19:49,813
What do you mean, my child?

449
00:19:49,897 --> 00:19:50,856
Are you kidding me?

450
00:19:50,939 --> 00:19:53,442
- Because Janine is my child.
- No. Atoy, I'm sure.

451
00:19:53,525 --> 00:19:55,152
I'll explain everything to you.

452
00:19:55,235 --> 00:19:57,738
- Janine isn't your child.
- What do you mean Ibyang-- Ibyang--

453
00:19:57,821 --> 00:20:00,073
Audrey herself told me.

454
00:20:00,157 --> 00:20:01,825
[sentimental music playing]

455
00:20:02,534 --> 00:20:04,036
[car blips]

456
00:20:04,119 --> 00:20:07,539
[sentimental music playing]

457
00:20:09,124 --> 00:20:12,669
[phone ringing]

458
00:20:14,588 --> 00:20:15,672
Hello?

459
00:20:15,756 --> 00:20:17,257
[Audrey] <i>Ah, Olga?</i>

460
00:20:17,341 --> 00:20:18,467
Who's this?

461
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:21,011
It's Audrey.

462
00:20:21,094 --> 00:20:23,597
I got your number from Miss Cita.

463
00:20:25,599 --> 00:20:28,143
She said you're with those rescuing Atoy.

464
00:20:28,227 --> 00:20:33,190
Ah, yes. I'm with Uno
and the extraction team.

465
00:20:33,857 --> 00:20:36,944
[Audrey in English] <i>I just</i>
<i>want to wish you well.</i>

466
00:20:38,695 --> 00:20:40,364
[in English] Please bring him back.

467
00:20:42,074 --> 00:20:43,492
I need Atoy.

468
00:20:44,826 --> 00:20:47,704
We need to find our child.

469
00:20:48,288 --> 00:20:49,289
Wait.

470
00:20:49,373 --> 00:20:51,667
Isn't Janine your child?

471
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:56,088
Before we came here,

472
00:20:56,964 --> 00:20:58,757
I found out Red deceived me.

473
00:20:59,967 --> 00:21:02,678
My brother was the one searching
for our missing child.

474
00:21:04,179 --> 00:21:05,889
The child they introduced to us was fake.

475
00:21:07,891 --> 00:21:11,770
Only a few of you know
that Janine isn't really my child.

476
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:16,525
But Atoy also needs to know the truth.

477
00:21:19,027 --> 00:21:24,116
[sentimental music playing]

478
00:21:30,163 --> 00:21:33,417
Atoy, you're Ibyang's father.

479
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:36,211
And Ibyang needs to know all about this.

480
00:21:42,384 --> 00:21:45,846
[in English] Glory be to the Father,
and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit.

481
00:21:45,929 --> 00:21:48,223
[in English] As it was
in the beginning is now,

482
00:21:48,307 --> 00:21:50,434
and ever shall be, world without end.

483
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:51,518
Amen.

484
00:21:55,605 --> 00:22:00,277
[light music playing]

485
00:22:24,468 --> 00:22:25,677
Tatoy?!

486
00:22:33,226 --> 00:22:39,357
[sentimental music playing]

487
00:22:59,586 --> 00:23:01,338
[music fades]

488
00:23:02,005 --> 00:23:03,131
Tatoy.

489
00:23:04,174 --> 00:23:05,717
You're back!

490
00:23:07,928 --> 00:23:08,929
Thank you, Lord!

491
00:23:09,012 --> 00:23:10,847
Thank you, thank you!

492
00:23:11,932 --> 00:23:13,100
[sobs]

493
00:23:15,477 --> 00:23:16,770
[sobbing]

494
00:23:17,479 --> 00:23:18,355
Why…

495
00:23:19,064 --> 00:23:21,149
Why are you crying?

496
00:23:22,192 --> 00:23:23,568
Shouldn't you be

497
00:23:24,361 --> 00:23:25,737
happy?

498
00:23:26,696 --> 00:23:28,782
I'm happy. I'm happy, Ibyang.

499
00:23:28,865 --> 00:23:30,617
[sniffles] There's…

500
00:23:31,243 --> 00:23:32,369
There's…

501
00:23:33,161 --> 00:23:35,330
[sniffles] There's something
I brought for you.

502
00:23:36,206 --> 00:23:38,708
[Ibyang] Why do you have that?

503
00:23:38,792 --> 00:23:40,710
[Ibyang] I gave that to Mama Olga.

504
00:23:41,753 --> 00:23:45,006
Eh, Olga gave it to me.

505
00:23:46,424 --> 00:23:48,552
She admitted the truth to me.

506
00:23:50,804 --> 00:23:52,931
That she isn't your real mother.

507
00:23:54,391 --> 00:23:56,017
She only pretended.

508
00:23:57,269 --> 00:23:58,228
Huh?

509
00:24:00,647 --> 00:24:03,441
[sobs] Don't worry about that.

510
00:24:03,525 --> 00:24:07,362
[sniffles] She also
told me the truth, Ibyang.

511
00:24:09,156 --> 00:24:11,700
She told me who…

512
00:24:11,783 --> 00:24:14,953
who your real parents are…

513
00:24:16,705 --> 00:24:20,375
and who your real father is.

514
00:24:23,295 --> 00:24:25,630
What do you mean?

515
00:24:27,465 --> 00:24:31,928
[sentimental music playing]

516
00:24:43,398 --> 00:24:45,442
Whoever holds this…

517
00:24:47,736 --> 00:24:50,530
will make you happy

518
00:24:50,614 --> 00:24:52,741
because he is your family.

519
00:24:52,824 --> 00:24:58,371
[music swells]

520
00:25:07,130 --> 00:25:10,091
You're my family?

521
00:25:10,175 --> 00:25:12,552
[music fades]

522
00:25:12,636 --> 00:25:14,471
Yes. Yes, Ibyang.

523
00:25:14,554 --> 00:25:16,264
[sobbing]

524
00:25:17,849 --> 00:25:20,936
You're my father?

525
00:25:23,730 --> 00:25:25,273
- [Ibyang sobs]
- Me.

526
00:25:27,609 --> 00:25:33,448
[sentimental music playing]

527
00:25:49,047 --> 00:25:51,591
- [electronic blipping]
- [tense music playing]

528
00:25:51,675 --> 00:25:53,385
May you be given a long time

529
00:25:53,468 --> 00:25:54,844
to be with them.

530
00:25:54,928 --> 00:25:56,221
I need your help.

531
00:25:56,304 --> 00:25:57,597
Your new mission.

532
00:25:58,181 --> 00:26:00,475
The corrupt mayor
who is the bagman of senators.

533
00:26:00,558 --> 00:26:01,768
[Mercado] You need to find him.

534
00:26:02,560 --> 00:26:05,105
[Siony] We really need to celebrate this!

535
00:26:05,188 --> 00:26:06,648
[Siony] Not just Atoy's safety,

536
00:26:06,731 --> 00:26:08,566
but also, the safety of Tabang Lupa!

537
00:26:08,650 --> 00:26:09,693
- Exactly!
- [cheering]

538
00:26:09,776 --> 00:26:10,777
- I have an idea!
- [Nestor] What?

539
00:26:10,860 --> 00:26:11,778
[T-Bak] <i>Boodle fight!</i>

540
00:26:11,861 --> 00:26:13,154
[Atoy] Oh? What's happening?

541
00:26:14,489 --> 00:26:15,949
[Emerson] Hey! Look, Atoy is here!

542
00:26:16,032 --> 00:26:20,161
Atoy! Atoy! Atoy! Atoy!

543
00:26:20,245 --> 00:26:22,789
Oh, there. That insect
on your face is gone.

544
00:26:22,872 --> 00:26:24,332
[REd] Don't move too much.

545
00:26:24,416 --> 00:26:26,126
I'll have a hard time killing you.

546
00:26:26,209 --> 00:26:27,335
Insect?

547
00:26:27,419 --> 00:26:31,631
Yes, like a green firefly
that keeps moving.

548
00:26:32,215 --> 00:26:33,466
[Peping] You didn't feel it?

549
00:26:33,550 --> 00:26:35,468
‪UP NEXT

550
00:26:35,552 --> 00:26:38,471
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

551
00:26:40,056 --> 00:26:41,558
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

552
00:26:41,641 --> 00:26:42,976
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
